{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-140851" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-140851" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-6-5+4 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-140851" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "63ae5446cd981c304159deb63b4bd4953b6eca97263bf349f940f91d83211791"} {"question" "q-140851" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-140851" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "-7"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-140851" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-140852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-140852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1+(-6)\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =3-12+20 \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-140852" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "63ae5446cd981c304159deb63b4bd4953b6eca97263bf349f940f91d83211791"} {"question" "q-140852" "