thacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93968" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "63ae5446cd981c304159deb63b4bd4953b6eca97263bf349f940f91d83211791"} {"question" "q-93968" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93968" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93968" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$   Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-6)+1\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & =12-8 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "63ae5446cd981c304159deb63b4bd4953b6eca97263bf349f940f91d83211791"} {"question" "q-93900" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93900" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-6"] ["math" "-7"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93900" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93971" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93971" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 6+(-4)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-20+18+8 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93971" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "63ae5446cd981c304159deb63b4bd4953b6eca97263bf349f940f91d83211791"} {"question" "q-93971" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93971" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93971" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the bilinear form $B(x,y),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(x,y)=2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-4{x}_{2}{y}_{3}+{x}_{3}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{3}{y}_{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(x,y)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given that \n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-4{x}_{2}{y}_{3}+{x}_{3}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{3}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 0-4\\cdot 2\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot 1-3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0-24-1-0 \\\\  & =-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "63ae5446cd981c304159deb63b4bd4953b6eca97263bf349f940f91d83211791"} {"question" "q-93981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-22"] ["math" "-25"] ["math" "-26"] ["math" "23"] ["math" "27"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-25"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}^{T}\\,Ay$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ay \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "63ae5446cd981c304159deb63b4bd4953b6eca97263bf349f940f91d83211791"} {"question" "q-93976" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93976" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-18"] ["math" "-42"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "22"] ["math" "24"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93976" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "24"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-140861" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}^{T}\\,Ay$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-140861" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ay \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 20\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =65.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-140861" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "63ae5446cd981c304159deb63b4bd4953b6eca97263bf349f940f91d83211791"} {"question" "q-140861" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-140861" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-25"] ["math" "105"] ["math" "25"] ["math" "65"] ["math" "70"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-140861" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "65"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,-2 & 4 \\\\ \\,2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}^{T}\\,Ay$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain   \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ay \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =28.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "63ae5446cd981c304159deb63b4bd4953b6eca97263bf349f940f91d83211791"} {"question" "q-93977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "22"] ["math" "28"] ["math" "32"] ["math" "36"] ["math" "42"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "28"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93916" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the bilinear form $B(x,y),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(x,y)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93916" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given that \n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 3+1\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 1\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =3+3-2-1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93916" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "63ae5446cd981c304159deb63b4bd4953b6eca97263bf349f940f91d83211791"} {"question" "q-93916" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93916" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93916" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-140863" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\,\\,-3 \\\\ \\,\\,3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-140863" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+(-3){x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & \\,\\,-3 \\\\ \\,\\,3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1}-3{y}_{2} \\\\ 3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(2{y}_{1}-3{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(3{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-140863" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "63ae5446cd981c304159deb63b4bd4953b6eca97263bf349f940f91d83211791"} {"question" "q-140863" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-140863" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}"] ["math" "2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-140863" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =(-2){x}_{1}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+(-1){x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =-2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ -{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(-2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2})+{x}_{2}(-{y}_{1}+3{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =-2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-93984" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "63ae5446cd981c304159d