\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & \\,\\,-2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=b=2.$ Finally,\n\n$$\na-b=2-2=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-94048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "63ae5446cd981c304159deb63b4bd4953b6eca97263bf349f940f91d83211791"} {"question" "q-94048" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-94048" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-94048" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-94045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)=-4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-5{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-94045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =-4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-5{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =(-4){x}_{1}{y}_{1}+\\,\\,3{x}_{1}{y}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,(-5){x}_{2}{y}_{1}\\,+(-2){x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-4$ and $b=3.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b=-4+3=-1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-94045" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "63ae5446cd981c304159deb63b4bd4953b6eca97263bf349f940f91d83211791"} {"question" "q-94045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-94045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "-7"] ["math" "-9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-94045" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-94040" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ 0 & b\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-94040" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+(-2){x}_{1}{y}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{2}{y}_{1}\\,+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1$ and $b=2.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b=1+2=3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-94040" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate 