rm corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+{x}_{3}{y}_{2}-3{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,2{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+1{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+(-3){x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-3.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+2+(-3)=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-94052" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "63ae5446cd981c304159deb63b4bd4953b6eca97263bf349f940f91d83211791"} {"question" "q-94052" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-94052" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "q-94052" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bb1af243bcecbe13d9c5c8e1e68728963196bf144c2474bc3b9639d91f20687"} {"question" "e-8160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The linear form $f(\\mathbf{x})$ is defined as $f(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{a} \\mathbf{x},$ where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/e104f037293e19fe2a12d9b2e14cc344d5cca06f933f393755cf03568b5702c0.png)  Evaluate the function when ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/8832f5ec6073de4098b3b0f856a3ab5e000926a9d09f76e87909adb67777cc17.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/example-8160.json" "file_sha256" "48d1d84fde39433c70420ebdd73f72cfcc918cf8296899834474e739d49beef0"} {"question" "e-8160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Substituting ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/4c5ce198c2271b51807f4c17fffdf4288c524ff73469196bd481dc489c5a0e40.png) we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-5)+0\\cdot 8+4\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-15+0+20 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/example-8160.json" "file_sha256" "48d1d84fde39433c70420ebdd73f72cfcc918cf8296899834474e739d49beef0"} {"question" "e-8161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the the bilinear form $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y}),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})= 2 x_1y_2 - x_2y_2 +3 x_2y_3-x_3y_1\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})$ when ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/dcea1a36972408a1f6a56577f61150bd8e4c2b91284820ca47c632a985d912ca.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/f9885ea740945a64e44931aca4befbd4022a84ae0fa1454627f2b44133eb4651.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/example-8161.json" "file_sha256" "2c1205be4adfad8cc518cb9dc002c63c1394bdeff062326015b8e7000e38b4b3"} {"question" "e-8161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given that \n\n$\\qquad$ ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/652258046237288de7102e402a266dd3afff1abfecf97aa2156a351a7611afb3.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/58ef5fbadaf595035dc902aac9b66bbce61fea79b6a4144ed060f0486dda982c.png) \n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-{x}_{3}{y}_{1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =4-2+3-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/example-8161.json" "file_sha256" "2c1205be4adfad8cc518cb9dc002c63c1394bdeff062326015b8e7000e38b4b3"} {"question" "e-8162" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/4dfdcd2e2f0d80ee8b6633b0dd4bc33b477b22e4db0f2ad36cbfa62eef702659.png)\nConsider the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/15fa693fff5bc0eb2a8851089612b5a3fb969c3fd5fbc7c0821e58e52ff4260d.png) above.  Write down a bilinear form ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/7c7f59284956b7a02d9d9d16387cfba529479fb49aa8efff3bfa908be0fbb04f.png) in terms of the components of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/ed54028979894fad0ac2b928c90c9eeea9361d1c8514fb61ee8ce28435ac2a5c.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/9849708035aaa18397dfafbbcdfeb923f576296406c494c30093477f6b2aaa33.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/example-8162.json" "file_sha256" "d30e69c0cba5a2fabd3538db7452f3266a0c7e3e37f367057aa9d39d18649551"} {"question" "e-8162" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/e8f54943816e5af3ad7a3b92ff68887d8126962ffcba1d3109d10390616d8a04.png) of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/3397629141c3034fbd4b5cd5bd8c554676175a4b1e3f5eccd26cc5d66ee1bec8.png) corresponds to the term ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/e4b6d1207e1c34e37c760af85eb4a4e5594e3db2da2c4ba4841a4106de188c1b.png) in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/734889027df1469d75a4506f295a277b908081224b5860ebf9ec8ea432053dd9.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/4ccd64cd17dd595c826e5a8bf13d4bf991c57d128d7a3fbca5a49eaf265f0867.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/example-8162.json" "file_sha256" "d30e69c0cba5a2fabd3538db7452f3266a0c7e3e37f367057aa9d39d18649551"} {"question" "e-8163" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix of the bilinear form $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y}) = 2x_1y_1 + 2x_2y_1 - x_3 y_2+2x_3y_3$ is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 & 0 \\\\ b & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & c & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/example-8163.json" "file_sha256" "41700ebfa251824912b44905152ec5fea5fdecba0504187da2af45fd74a91c83"} {"question" "e-8163" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Each term $a_{ij}x_i y_j$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry $a_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+(-1){x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/24b1e29dccdff51c2ca2c7780a8a5dfcf9c74ed91d48afdde8a14c5127f89ce1.png)\n\nTherefore, $a=2,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-1.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=2+2+(-1) = 3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/example-8163.json" "file_sha256" "41700ebfa251824912b44905152ec5fea5fdecba0504187da2af45fd74a91c83"}] "usage" {"e-8161" [] "e-8163" [] "e-8160" [] "q-94040" [] "e-8162" []} "basis" 1673 "retractions" [[17592186162541 :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}a & -2 \\\\ 0 & b\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x, y) = x_{1}y_{1} - 2x_{1}y_{2} + 2x_{2}y_{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a + b$?"] [17592186161704 :question/problem "The linear form $f(\\mathbf{x})$ is defined as $f(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{a} \\mathbf{x}$, where $\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$ Evaluate the function when $\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186161704 :question/worked-solution "Substituting $\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= ax \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot (-5) + 0 \\cdot 8 + 4 \\cdot 5 \\\\\n&=-15 + 0 + 20 \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186161705 :question/problem "Consider the the bilinear form $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})$, given by\n\n$B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})= 2 x_1y_2 - x_2y_2 +3 x_2y_3-x_3y_1$\n\nEvaluate $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})$ when $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186161705 :question/worked-solution "We are given that\n\n$\\qquad$ $\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2} \\\\ x_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}y_{1} \\\\ y_{2} \\\\ y_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nB(x, y) &= 2x_{1}y_{2} - x_{2}y_{2} + 3x_{2}y_{3} - x_{3}y_{1} \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 2 - 1 \\cdot 2 + 3 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 1 - (-1) \\cdot (-2) \\\\\n&= 4 - 2 + 3 - 2 \\\\\n&= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186161706 :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Write down a bilinear form $\\mathbf{x}^T \\! A \\mathbf{y}$ in terms of the components of $\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}y_{1} \\\\ y_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186161706 :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry $a_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term $a_{ij}x_i y_j$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{T}Ay &= 2x_{1}y_{1} + (-1)x_{1}y_{2} + 3x_{2}y_{1} + (-2)x_{2}y_{2} \\\\\n&= 2x_{1}y_{1} - x_{1}y_{2} + 3x_{2}y_{1} - 2x_{2}y_{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{T}Ay &= \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} & x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}y_{1} \\\\ y_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} & x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2y_{1} - y_{2} \\\\ 3y_{1} - 2y_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= x_{1}(2y_{1} - y_{2}) + x_{2}(3y_{1} - 2y_{2}) \\\\\n&= 2x_{1}y_{1} - x_{1}y_{2} + 3x_{2}y_{1} - 2x_{2}y_{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186161707 :question/problem "The matrix of the bilinear form $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y}) = 2x_1y_1 + 2x_2y_1 - x_3 y_2+2x_3y_3$ is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c$?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 & 0 \\\\ b & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & c & 2\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186161707 :question/worked-solution "Each term $a_{ij}x_i y_j$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry $a_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nB(x, y) &= 2x_{1}y_{1} + 2x_{2}y_{1} - x_{3}y_{2} + 2x_{3}y_{3} \\\\\n&= 2x_{1}y_{1} + 0x_{1}y_{2} + 0x_{1}y_{3} \\\\\n&= + 2x_{2}y_{1} + 0x_{2}y_{2} + 0x_{2}y_{3} \\\\\n&= + 0x_{3}y_{1} + (-1)x_{3}y_{2} + 2x_{3}y_{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=2$, $b=2$, and $c=-1$. Finally,\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+2+(-1) = 3\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186160879 17592186160880 17592186160881 17592186160882 17592186160883] "immutable_fields" [[17592186160878 :answer-field/correct] [17592186160878 :answer-field/id] [17592186160878 :answer-field/key] [17592186160878 :answer-